        <p>This instrument has no domain author yet. Someone who knows Indonesian regional economic statistics. The nowcast is 99.5% intercept and 41% worse than carrying last year forward; the Gibson relationship holds for kota and inverts for kabupaten. What is missing is why it inverts — whether BPS's GRDP methodology explains it, and what nightlights can honestly proxy in a country with this settlement pattern.</p>
